From: gahingwoo <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd: default to Panfrost when built with it

The wddm-mali-g52 build of this target is maliumd.dll, the UMD that
maliwddm names. Windows loads a UMD into every process that touches
D3D (explorer, the shell hosts, Direct2D users, DWM), and none of them
set GALLIUM_DRIVER. They got the default, softpipe, on a Mali adapter,
and softpipe's TGSI interpreter hit an assertion on a Direct2D shader
("mach->pc < (int) mach->NumInstructions" in tgsi_exec_machine_run).
explorer.exe, StartMenuExperienceHost, SearchHost and
ShellExperienceHost then aborted in a loop, about every 12 s
(c0000409/7 in ucrtbase, WER dumps of 2026-10-17).

Make Panfrost the default in a build that has it. GALLIUM_DRIVER still
overrides it, and if Panfrost cannot create a screen the existing
softpipe fallback is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: gahingwoo <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
---
 src/gallium/targets/d3d10umd/d3d10_gdi.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/targets/d3d10umd/d3d10_gdi.c b/src/gallium/targets/d3d10umd/d3d10_gdi.c
index bbd677f..73dfc2f 100644
--- a/src/gallium/targets/d3d10umd/d3d10_gdi.c
+++ b/src/gallium/targets/d3d10umd/d3d10_gdi.c
@@ -203,6 +203,12 @@ d3d10_create_screen(void)
 #else
    default_driver = "softpipe";
 #endif
+#ifdef GALLIUM_PANFROST
+   /* As maliumd.dll this UMD is loaded into processes that never set
+    * GALLIUM_DRIVER (explorer, DWM, every Direct2D user); on a Mali adapter
+    * they must get the Mali. */
+   default_driver = "panfrost";
+#endif
 
    driver = debug_get_option("GALLIUM_DRIVER", default_driver);
 
